      "journal": "Journal of Russian Laser Research",
      "notes": "Vol. 17, No. 4, pp. 332-345. Three-step AVLIS scheme: 6s2 1S0 -[555.648nm air]-> 6s6p 3P1 -[581.067nm air]-> (4f13 6s2 6p)(7/2,3/2)J=2 at 35196.98 cm^-1 -[582.79nm]-> autoionization at 52353 cm^-1. PRIMARY source of 581nm isotope shifts (Table 2, p.334-335): all-isotope shifts and 171/173Yb HFS components for the 6^3P1 -> (7/2,3/2)_2 transition, measured first in this paper. Table 1 (556nm isotope shifts) reproduces Broadhurst et al. 1974 and is attributed to that paper. Lifetime of (7/2,3/2)_2: 1.12+-0.05 us measured by luminescence dynamics (p.334). Dipole moment 6^3P1 -> (7/2,3/2)_2: 4.2e-30 C.m (p.334). Level energies from Martin, Zalubas, Hagan 1978 (ref [2]).",
